hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"317","We have Bandar Muhammad bin Bashar, we have Yahya bin Saeed, we have Ismail, we have Qais, he said: Jarir bin Abdullah said: We were sitting with the Prophet, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If you are able not to neglect the prayer before sunrise and before its setting.”"
"318","Bundar told us, Yahya told us, and Yazid bin Harun told us: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amara bin Ruwaiba, On the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever prays before the sun rises and before it sets, God will make him forbidden to the Fire.” A man from Basra said: I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"319","On the authority of Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Amara bin Ruwaybah, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “No one who prays before sunrise or before it sets will enter Hell.”"
"320","Narrated by Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, narrated by Shayban, narrated by Abdul-Malik bin Umair, who said: I heard Amara bin Ruwayba, saying: I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “No one who prays before the sunrise or its sunset will enter Hell.” Then a man from the people of Basra came to him and said: You heard this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness that you heard it."
